mod backend.optimizer.passes.registers;

import (
    std.io
)

/**
 * WHERE VALUES LIVE: the two passes that run last
 *
 * Every other pass changes WHAT the code computes with; these two decide
 * where the values are kept while it does - the part of a compiler the
 * textbook calls register allocation (the dragon book, 8.8). On this VM a
 * value has two possible homes: a slot of the function's frame, or, for the
 * moment between two instructions, the register it was computed in.
 *
 * They run after every pass that changes code, in this order
 * (optimizer.sharp, `optimize_program`):
 *
 *      slot_packing.sharp          values that are never alive at the same time share one slot,
 *                                  so the frame is small (frame size is recursion depth here)
 *      register_hand_off.sharp     a value read only by the very next instruction is never
 *                                  stored into its slot at all
 *      registers.sharp             this front door
 *
 * (module `backend.optimizer.passes.registers`)
 */
